---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy | Thornveil">
  <section class="tv-section pt-s-11">
    <div class="tv-container max-w-3xl">
      <h1 class="tv-h1 mt-s-3 reveal reveal-delay-1">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="font-mono text-step--1 tracking-[0.10em] uppercase text-text-3 mt-s-3 reveal reveal-delay-2">
        Configuration reviewed September 15, 2026 · operational details pending confirmation
      </p>

      <div class="mt-s-7 space-y-s-7 text-step-0 text-text-2 reveal reveal-delay-2">
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-step-1 text-text mb-s-3" style="font-variation-settings: 'wdth' 125;">Summary</h2>
          <p>
            This notice covers the Thornveil website, not deployments of Thornveil products.
            Thornveil is operated by its owner in Florida and is intended for a US audience.
            The current site has no account registration, contact form, or advertising scripts.
            It loads Plausible Analytics and Google Fonts, so visiting a page can send technical request
            data to those services and the hosting provider. Contact is handled separately through email.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-step-1 text-text mb-s-3" style="font-variation-settings: 'wdth' 125;">Analytics</h2>
          <p>
            The site is configured to load Plausible's hosted analytics script for thornveil.ai.
            According to
            <a href="https://plausible.io/data-policy" class="text-signal-text underline underline-offset-4 decoration-1">Plausible's data policy</a>,
            it measures page URLs, referral sources, browser, operating system, device type, and approximate
            location (country, region, and city) in aggregate. Requests include an IP address and user agent;
            Plausible says it uses these to generate a daily identifier without storing the raw values.
            It says it uses no cookies or persistent identifiers, does not track visitors across days or
            websites, and processes visitor data in the EU. These are the provider's descriptions,
            not a guarantee of this site's legal compliance.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-s-3">
            The owner reports not having set up a Plausible account and reports observing the script
            load on the live site. Loading the script alone does not establish whether analytics events
            are accepted or retained. Account ownership, report access and sharing, exports,
            retention, and deletion settings remain unverified.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-step-1 text-text mb-s-3" style="font-variation-settings: 'wdth' 125;">Hosting and fonts</h2>
          <p>
            Based on the owner's live-account and response-header checks, Netlify provides hosting,
            CDN delivery, and DNS for this site. Hosting providers may process access and security logs,
            including IP addresses, browser details, requested URLs, and request times.
            <a href="https://www.netlify.com/privacy/" class="text-signal-text underline underline-offset-4 decoration-1">Netlify's privacy statement</a>
            describes its collection and processing of device and service data. The owner reports
            that no Netlify Log Drains are connected. This does not mean Netlify keeps no logs or
            that no other copies exist. Logging settings, applicable retention and deletion periods,
            and any additional services remain to be confirmed.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-s-3">
            Fonts are requested from Google Fonts. Google's
            <a href="https://developers.google.com/fonts/faq/privacy" class="text-signal-text underline underline-offset-4 decoration-1">Fonts privacy FAQ</a>
            explains that these requests include the visitor's IP address, the requested URL, and headers
            such as the user agent and referrer. Google says the Fonts API does not set or log cookies
            and does not use this information for targeted advertising.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-step-1 text-text mb-s-3" style="font-variation-settings: 'wdth' 125;">Cookies and browser storage</h2>
          <p>
            The current site code does not set cookies or use browser storage for tracking.
            That statement does not cover additional services a hosting provider may enable or
            external sites you choose to visit. Those services have their own policies.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-step-1 text-text mb-s-3" style="font-variation-settings: 'wdth' 125;">Email contact and retention</h2>
          <p>
            Email links open your email app, sometimes with a subject and message template. Nothing
            is submitted through a website form. If you send the email, Thornveil receives your address,
            message, and any attachments so it can respond; email providers also process the correspondence.
            The contact mailbox uses Google Workspace. The owner confirms that only they have access
            to the mailbox; this does not exclude processing by the email provider.
            A retention schedule and deletion process have not yet been established for this notice.
            Please do not send classified, controlled, or sensitive
            information through this public contact channel.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-s-3">
            Google's
            <a href="https://support.google.com/vault/answer/2535539?hl=en" class="text-signal-text underline underline-offset-4 decoration-1">Gmail retention documentation</a>
            explains that, where Google Vault is used, retention rules and legal holds can prevent
            permanent deletion. The owner reports an active Google Workspace Business Plus subscription,
            which includes Vault. Specific Vault rules and holds, backups, automatic deletion,
            forwarding, and connected third-party app access have not been verified.
            No provider default is presented here as Thornveil's retention policy.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-step-1 text-text mb-s-3" style="font-variation-settings: 'wdth' 125;">Details awaiting owner confirmation</h2>
          <p>
            Before treating this notice as final, the owner needs to verify any additional providers,
            analytics collection and access, and retention and deletion practices for email, analytics,
            and logs. The applicable legal requirements and a documented process for privacy requests
            also remain to be established. Operating in Florida and targeting a US audience alone
            do not determine which privacy laws apply.
            No specific retention period, response deadline, or compliance certification is asserted here.
            Product data handling depends on the product, deployment settings, and connected services;
            consult the relevant product documentation and agreement rather than this website notice.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-step-1 text-text mb-s-3" style="font-variation-settings: 'wdth' 125;">Contact</h2>
          <p>
            Questions about this policy:
            {' '}<a href="mailto:jesse@thornveil.ai" class="text-signal-text underline underline-offset-4 decoration-1">
              jesse@thornveil.ai
            </a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
